7s suggestion to transform \"Projetos / Participe\" into \"Eventos,\" or create separate highlights.\n\n\n**Defining Instagram Highlights Strategy**\n\nI\u0027m currently focused on strategizing a functional and strategic Instagram Highlights layout for ACIRV. The immediate need is to define the ideal structure, keeping in mind the association\u0027s goals for promoting itself on Instagram. I need to consider current highlights and identify a better system.\n\n\n**Structuring Instagram Highlights**\n\nI\u0027ve been analyzing the existing Instagram Highlights, specifically the titles and content of each. I\u0027m building a more robust structure, separating current topics into \"Testimonials\", \"Products \u0026 Services (Discover)\", \"Projects (Participate)\", \"Sectoral Nuclei (Learn More)\", \"SUDO EXPO (2026)\", and \"ACIRV (Join Us!)\". My analysis includes identifying the target audiences and how each highlight serves them.\n\n\n**Clarifying Highlight Titles**\n\nI\u0027ve realized the current Instagram Highlights use confusing titles. The text beneath each highlight, which is the actual title, uses verbs like \"Conheça\" and \"Participe,\" making them unclear. It\u0027s much better to have the highlight title be the subject, matching the icon, like \"Soluções\" or \"Serviços\". I recommend a naming overhaul, for a clearer user experience. Also, the current \"Associe-se!\" highlight, currently a facade picture, needs content.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Highlight Placement**\n\nOkay, I\u0027m now structuring the Instagram Highlights with strategic priority in mind. \"Associe-se!\" should be the leftmost highlight, representing the primary conversion funnel. I\u0027m thinking of \"Quem Somos\" to showcase the association. Following that, \"Soluções,\" \"Núcleos,\" and \"Eventos\" seem like the best arrangement. This focuses on guiding users logically through information.\n\n\n**Adding Key Highlights**\n\nI\u0027m now adding more key highlights, specifically for social proof with \"Depoimentos\" and \"Parceiros.\" I need to check the current highlights, as they currently use \"Depoimentos\", and ensure that the title below the bubble uses that term, as well. Also, ACIRV\u0027s arbitration chamber, \"CCCA / Mediação,\" deserves a dedicated highlight. Finally, I\u0027m analyzing which existing highlights to keep and rename. \"Produtos e Serviços\" should become \"Serviços\" or \"Soluções,\" and \"Núcleos Setoriais\" should be renamed to \"Núcleos\".\n\n\n**Refining Highlight Content**\n\nI\u0027m now focused on the content within each Instagram Highlight, especially \"SudoExpo\" and \"Associe-se!\". For \"SudoExpo,\" the title needs a clarifying update; I suggest \"SudoExpo\" or \"SudoExpo 2026.\" \"Associe-se!\" requires a complete content overhaul, ditching the generic photo for a compelling pitch on benefits, the joining process, and a CTA. Furthermore, \"Projetos / Participe\" is too vague. I recommend renaming it to \"Eventos\" or \"Agenda,\" as ACIRV\u0027s events are key.\n\n\n**Prioritizing New Highlights**\n\nI\u0027m now prioritizing the new highlight additions, evaluating their strategic importance. I\u0027m focusing on \"Câmara de Mediação\" and \"Conecta Saúde\" as potential new highlights. \"Câmara de Mediação\" has clear revenue generation potential, so I am considering giving it its own highlight, or a prominent placement inside \"Serviços\". I\u0027m also determining whether \"Conecta Saúde\" is a product/service that needs a temporary campaign highlight.\n\n\n**Refining Highlight Structure**\n\nI\u0027m now prioritizing keeping the total number of visible highlights to six or seven max. Instagram only shows a limited number without scrolling, so that number feels like a sweet spot. I\u0027m considering grouping content under \"Serviços\" or \"Eventos\" to avoid clutter. I realize Instagram\u0027s goal is to serve as ACIRV\u0027s digital headquarters, and the highlights need to serve existing members and attract new ones.\n\n\n**Defining Highlight Content**\n\nI\u0027m now focusing on refining the content within the key highlights. \"Associe-se!\" needs an urgent overhaul, transforming from a generic image to a compelling pitch outlining the association\u0027s value, the joining process, and a clear call to action. I also plan to rename \"Produtos e Serviços\" to \"Serviços\" and \"Núcleos Setoriais\" to \"Núcleos\" for a clearer user experience. \"Projetos\" should be renamed to \"Eventos\" to represent ACIRV events.\n\n\n**Evaluating Highlight Content**\n\nI\u0027m now prioritizing the \"Eventos\" highlight, specifically the photos and calendar updates. Since these events happen frequently, the highlight will need constant refreshing with photos and a calendar. Also, the \"SudoExpo\" highlight should be renamed to either \"SudoExpo\" or \"SudoExpo 2026\" for clarity. The \"Depoimentos\" highlight will be kept, aiming to gather testimonials from local business owners who have seen results with ACIRV. I will also evaluate ACIRV\u0027s Câmara de Mediação, which could be a high-value service.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Highlight Order**\n\nI\u0027m now determining the ideal order for the Instagram Highlights, viewing it as a conversion funnel. I\u0027m prioritizing \"Associe-se!\" as the first highlight, followed by \"Serviços,\" then \"Núcleos,\" \"Eventos,\" and finally \"SudoExpo\". This aims to guide visitors through ACIRV\u0027s value proposition strategically. I\u0027m emphasizing that, on Instagram, the most recently updated highlights appear on the left, but I will be intentionally organizing them in this suggested order, to keep the flow consistent.\n\n\n**Developing Highlight Content**\n\nI\u0027m now detailing the content structure for each highlight, aiming for a 3-5 story sequence. For \"Associe-se!,\" I\u0027m crafting a compelling narrative: an introductory video, benefits explained, a happy member testimonial, and a clear call to action. \"Serviços\" will highlight solutions, commercial benefits like SPC/Serasa, and health \u0026 wellbeing partnerships.\n\n\n**Structuring Highlight Content**\n\nI\u0027m now outlining content for the \"Núcleos,\" \"Eventos,\" and \"SudoExpo\" highlights. \"Núcleos\" will introduce sectoral groups, highlight active ones with visuals, and explain participation. \"Eventos\" will showcase networking, training sessions, and offer a monthly agenda. \"SudoExpo\" will explain the fair, present statistics, and promote exhibitor opportunities. I\u0027m focusing on concise stories with clear calls to action.\n\n\n**Refining Highlight Content Strategy**\n\nI\u0027m now diving into the specific content for the new highlights I am working on. The \"SudoExpo\" highlight sequence will focus on promoting exhibitor spaces, providing general information about the event (date, location, how to participate). If I decide to dedicate a highlight to it, \"Mediação\" will explain the chamber, its advantages, potential uses, and a direct call to action. I\u0027ll also start gathering testimonials for the \"Depoimentos\" highlight.\n\n\n**Refining Highlight Updates**\n\nI\u0027m now focusing on keeping highlights fresh. \"Eventos\" and \"SudoExpo\" require frequent updates; I plan for monthly or bi-weekly maintenance. The ideal length is 7-10 stories per highlight to avoid overwhelming users. Also, I\u0027m reminding the team that the most recently updated highlight goes to the left, and I\u0027ll be sure to update key ones like \"Serviços\" and \"Associe-se!\" with a quick story to keep them in place. The cover icons must be legible.\n\n\n",
